    {
      "id": "l1",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "The 1–2% rule",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "The 1–2% rule"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/1-zasada-1-2-procent.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In a single trade you risk at most **1–2% of your whole portfolio**."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "With 5,000 € that's at most **50–100 € of loss** on one idea. Even 10 losing trades in a row won't knock you out of the game."
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "text": "Professionals survive not because they're always right, but because their **losses are small**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
    {
      "id": "l2",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "Position size",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Position size"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/2-wielkosc-pozycji.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Position size comes from **how much you want to risk** and where your Stop-Loss is. Example:"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                "Portfolio: **5,000 €**",
                "1% risk: **50 €**",
                "Stop-Loss: 5% below the entry price",
                "Position: **1,000 €** (5% of 1,000 € = 50 €)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "text": "First you set the **risk**, only then the amount you buy – never the other way round."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
    {
      "id": "l3",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "Safe training ground",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Safe training ground"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/3-bezpieczny-poligon.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Before you risk your own money, test your strategy on a **demo account** or in a simulator with virtual cash."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "You'll see how orders, Stop-Loss and **your own emotions** work when you lose – and it costs nothing."
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "text": "Strategy not making money on demo for a few months? It **won't start** with real money either."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
